### a) Selection Sort Algorithm & Implementation (5 Marks)

```text
Algorithm SELECTION_SORT(A, n)
[Sorts A[0 .. n - 1] in ascending order]

1. For i = 0 to n - 2 do
   a) min_idx = i
   b) For j = i + 1 to n - 1 do
          If A[j] < A[min_idx] then
              min_idx = j
   c) If min_idx != i then
          Swap A[i] and A[min_idx]
2. Return
```

```c
#include <stdio.h>

void selectionSort(int a[], int n) {
    for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
        int min_idx = i;
        for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
            if (a[j] < a[min_idx]) min_idx = j;
        }
        if (min_idx != i) {
            int tmp = a[i]; a[i] = a[min_idx]; a[min_idx] = tmp;
        }
    }
}

int main(void) {
    int a[] = {29, 10, 14, 37, 13};
    selectionSort(a, 5);
    printf("%d %d %d %d %d\n", a[0], a[1], a[2], a[3], a[4]);
    return 0;
}
```

- **Complexity:** Always performs `n(n - 1) / 2 =` **`Theta(n²)` comparisons** (best, average, and worst case), **`<= n - 1` swaps**, and **`O(1)` extra space**.

### b) Minimum Spanning Tree Using Kruskal's Algorithm (5 Marks)

- **Vertices:** `V = {A, B, C, D, E, F}` (`|V| = 6`, so MST needs `|V| - 1 =` **`5` edges**).
- **Sorted Non-Decreasing Edge List (`9` Edges):**
  `D-F (1)`, `A-B (2)`, `A-C (2)`, `B-E (2)`, `C-B (3)`, `C-F (3)`, `D-E (4)`, `C-D (5)`, `B-D (6)`.

| Step | Candidate Edge | Weight | Cycle Check (`Disjoint Components`) | Decision |
|:-:|---|:-:|---|---|
| 1 | `D - F` | `1` | `{D}` != `{F}` -> merge `{D, F}` | **Accept (`1/5`)** |
| 2 | `A - B` | `2` | `{A}` != `{B}` -> merge `{A, B}` | **Accept (`2/5`)** |
| 3 | `A - C` | `2` | `{A, B}` != `{C}` -> merge `{A, B, C}` | **Accept (`3/5`)** |
| 4 | `B - E` | `2` | `{A, B, C}` != `{E}` -> merge `{A, B, C, E}` | **Accept (`4/5`)** |
| 5 | `C - B` | `3` | Both `C` & `B` in `{A, B, C, E}` (**forms cycle `A-B-C-A`**) | **Reject** |
| 6 | `C - F` | `3` | `{A, B, C, E}` != `{D, F}` -> connects all `6` vertices | **Accept (`5/5` — Stop)** |

```ascii
  Final Kruskal MST:
  [E]--(2)--[B]--(2)--[A]--(2)--[C]--(3)--[F]--(1)--[D]
```

- **MST Edges:** `{ (D, F), (A, B), (A, C), (B, E), (C, F) }`
- **Minimum Spanning Tree Total Weight:** `1 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 3 =` **`10`**.

